Z||000006||Jefrysuko||11-28-2001||12:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>Jeff, where would I find those on the car?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>They are listed on a little piece of paper about 4" by 6".  If you open the hood and stand by the front drivers side wheel and look down it will be right there.  It is basically on the backside of the front driverside wheelwell.  There will be a couple dozen codes all three characters long.  eg. WS6<P>Did you understand that i'm not sure if I did  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||CJ||11-28-2001||09:31 AM||||I agree that the 3rd and 4th characters should be "PG"...indicates a Fiero GT Coupe.<P>The check digit of the vin located in position 9 can be either a number or the letter "X".<P>If you change the 3rd character in this VIN to a P, the check digit of "X" shown is correct.<P>The check digit is used to verify that the VIN does not contain any errors, such as the "BG" that was originally thought to be here.  With the "BG" in the VIN, the check digit calculates to be a "7", while the VIN itself showed an "X", so I knew there was an error in the VIN.<P>I use a simple Excel file to verify the VIN check digits as specified in the Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Regulation 565.||||reg||1
Z||000008||TRiAD||11-28-2001||08:00 PM||||I'll try to get those build codes for you...<P>||||reg||1
